The '''PYRAMID30 Okaiken''' is a chart that ranks the best-performing singles in [[Okaiken]]. Its data, published by Nikkan Sports & Entertainment magazine, KTK Group and compiled by Okaiken Pyramid Records, is based collectively on each single's weekly physical and digital sales, as well as radio airplay and streaming. PYRAMID30 Okaiken is a subsidiary of Pyramid Records but acts as a separate organization. The weekly charts are updated every Sunday at 11:45 in the morning (UTC +9). The following lists all of the number one singles of the PYRAMID30 Okaiken for 2020.

In the timeline of Okaiken history, 2020 was the "Year of the Auteur" ({{nihongo|Sakka no Toshi|作家の年}}). Unlike other regions of Adonia, Okaiken avoided the global pandemic, allowing the highly anticipated [[2020 Okami Olympics]] to proceed as scheduled in July. This created a massive economic and cultural boom, fueling a fierce battle for chart dominance between experimental Rock and avant-garde Hip-Hop.

Critics retrospectively refer to this year as the rise of "Crit-Core" (or "Fantano-Core"), where artistically challenging acts like [[Dos Monos]], [[Haru Nemuri]], and [[GEZAN]] achieved mainstream number-one hits, displacing traditional pop. The charts were defined by high-concept albums, genre-bending collaborations, and the massive Olympic anthem by [[millennium parade]].

